     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"Data exfiltration is not reachable. Every exfiltration technique (exfiltrate_db, exfiltrate_fileserver, exfiltrate_backup) requires admin on the db, fileserver or backup host. Each of those needs a foothold on that host. Each foothold (auth_db, auth_fileserver, auth_backup) requires stolen_dbadmin. stolen_dbadmin can only come from dump_dbadmin_dc or dump_dbadmin_adfs, which need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, which can only be gained through auth_dc or auth_adfs. Both of those require NOT mfa_admin, and mfa:admin is deployed. The earlier stages still work: phishing gives a workstation foothold and stolen_user, pivot_internal works because there is no segmentation, auth_appserver works, and kerberoasting gives stolen_admin. However, the MFA requirement on admin authentication cuts the chain at the DC/ADFS step, so stolen_dbadmin and every exfiltration technique stay unreachable.\"}"
    }
